---
/**
 * Where to get help.
 *
 * The channel comes from SECURITY.md and the documentation, both of which say the item's
 * CodeCanyon comments page. If that changes it changes here and in several documentation
 * pages at once - flagged in owner-todo.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
---

<Base
	title="Support — Ultimate Client Manager"
	description="Where to get help with Ultimate Client Manager, what to check first, and how to report a security problem."
	current="/support/"
>
	<section class="hero">
		<div class="wrap narrow">
			<p class="kicker">Support</p>
			<h1>Getting help</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				Most problems people hit are covered in the documentation, and the troubleshooting
				page usually names the exact setting or file permission at fault.
			</p>
			<div class="actions">
				<a class="button quiet" href="/docs/reference/troubleshooting/">Troubleshooting</a>
				<a class="button quiet" href="/docs/install/installing/">Installation guide</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="tint">
		<div class="wrap narrow">
			<h2>Before you ask</h2>
			<p>Three things resolve most reports immediately, so include them:</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Which PHP version your host runs.</li>
				<li>Whether the site is on Apache or nginx.</li>
				<li>
					What the page actually did — a blank screen, an error message, or the wrong
					result. These have different causes and
					<a href="/docs/reference/troubleshooting/">troubleshooting</a> treats them
					separately.
				</li>
			</ol>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section>
		<div class="wrap narrow">
			<h2>Where to ask</h2>
			<p>
				Support is through the item's comments page on CodeCanyon:
				<a href="https://codecanyon.net/item/freelance-project-invoice-crm/2621629">
					the Freelance Project Invoice CRM item
				</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
				<Placeholder what="confirm the support channel and any response time you want to promise" />
			</p>

			<h2>Reporting a security problem</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Not in the public comments.</strong> Open a security advisory on the
				<a href="https://github.com/dtbaker/ucm">GitHub repository</a>, or contact the
				vendor privately through CodeCanyon. Include the version, the steps to reproduce,
				and what an attacker gets out of it.
			</p>
			<p>
				Confirmed issues are fixed and flagged as security fixes in the changelog that
				ships with the release.
			</p>

			<h2>Help inside the application</h2>
			<p>
				The help button on any screen opens the documentation article for that screen.
				It reads a copy of the documentation that ships inside your download, so it works
				with no internet connection at all, and fetches a newer version only when you open
				an article and only if you have left that switched on.
				<a href="/docs/using/help-system/">What that request contains</a> is written down
				in full, because it used to contain far more than it should have.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
